Read closed shards on a fresh start (no shard state from a checkpoint).
Upstream v2.0.0 (dd327d1) marks a closed shard it has not seen before as
ShardEnd, so a query that starts on a stream that already has a closed shard
skips that shard's retained records: data loss on a first start or a
recovery run after a reshard. Later batches keep the upstream rule.
Found by clavesa make test-stream (2026-11-01).

--- a/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/connector/kinesis/ShardSyncer.scala
+++ b/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/connector/kinesis/ShardSyncer.scala
@@ -274,7 +274,21 @@
       } else {
         AddShardInfoForAncestors(shardId,
           latestShards, initialPosition, prevShardsList, newShardsInfoMap, memoizationContext)
-        newShardsInfoMap.put(shardId, new ShardInfo(shardId, new ShardEnd()))
+        // clavesa patch: on a fresh start (no shard state from a checkpoint)
+        // a closed shard still holds records until the stream retention
+        // expires them, so start it at the initial position. Upstream marks
+        // it ShardEnd, which skips those records when a query starts after a
+        // reshard. Later batches keep the upstream rule: a closed shard that
+        // is missing from the previous offsets was already read to its end
+        // (finished shards drop out of the offsets).
+        if (prevShardsList.isEmpty) {
+          if (!newShardsInfoMap.contains(shardId)) {
+            newShardsInfoMap.put(shardId,
+              new ShardInfo(shardId, initialPosition.shardPosition(shardId)))
+          }
+        } else {
+          newShardsInfoMap.put(shardId, new ShardInfo(shardId, new ShardEnd()))
+        }
       }
     }
   }
